  "details": "I uploaded an Excellent avatar with 16 VRC Raycast components to force it down to Very Poor rank. My Avatars list reports it as Excellent on the server-side (?) in-app, but the client-side and the avatar SDK reports it as Very Poor. It's Excellent on Windows otherwise.\n\nSample affected private avatars uploaded by me:\n\n- [Robot （Very Poor raycasts）](https://vrchat.com/home/avatar/avtr_714e8215-60da-434e-8d81-5264345f0465) (`avtr_714e8215-60da-434e-8d81-5264345f0465`)\n\n- [Robot （Poor raycasts）](https://vrchat.com/home/avatar/avtr_bf5f2792-a8e0-4eef-8b9c-ff4545b23528) (`avtr_bf5f2792-a8e0-4eef-8b9c-ff4545b23528`) - the only difference to the above is this one is rated Poor on the server-side (9 VRC Raycast components) instead of Very Poor with 16 VRC Raycasts.\n\nExpected behavior: Very Poor in both client-side and server-side indication. \"Very Poor\" icon in My Avatars list.\n\nActual behavior: The avatar is ranked Excellent server-side & Very Poor on the client-side simultaneously, and I'm guessing it behaves like a Very Poor avatar (?). The avatars list displays a green \"Excellent\" icon.\n\nThis is reproducible in both the Default Public Version branch (Build 1820) and open-beta branch (Build 1832). I've included bug repro videos and output logs for both.",
